The role&nbsp; 

We're hiring our technical lead to own the architecture and delivery of our unified product platform - bringing several mature in-house applications together into one cohesive, multi-tenant, cloud-hosted portal for external clients. You will set the technical direction, lead the existing development team, and be the person who takes this platform from internal tooling to a secure, scalable product that trading firms pay for. &nbsp; 

This is a spearhead role. You'll report directly to the founders, shape the architecture from the ground up, and grow the team as the business scales. &nbsp; 

What you'll do&nbsp; 

- Own the end-to-end technical architecture for a multi-product, multi-tenant platform - frontend, containerised backends, shared services, and data isolation. &nbsp; 
 - Lead and mentor the existing engineering team; raise the bar on engineering practice, DevOps, and delivery. &nbsp; 
 - Design for commercial reality: client onboarding, security, auditability, and the realities of selling software to institutional buyers. &nbsp; 
 - Partner with the founders on the product roadmap and the build-to-revenue journey. &nbsp; 
 - Make the pragmatic calls - robust where it matters, lean where it doesn't - to ship on time without over-engineering. &nbsp; 
 - Streamlining processes using AI&nbsp; 

What you'll bring&nbsp; 

- 5-10+ years in software engineering, with real architectural ownership of a commercial product. &nbsp; 
 - Experience taking a B2B or SaaS product from build through to paying customers - you understand that how software is sold and shapes how it's built. &nbsp; 
 - Proven team leadership: you've led developers, set standards, and grown people. &nbsp; 
 - Strong foundations in cloud (AWS or equivalent), containerisation, multi-tenancy, and secure data handling. &nbsp; 
 - Comfort operating in a fast-moving, high-ownership environment with direct impact. &nbsp; Nice to have&nbsp; 

- Background in trading, capital markets, or financial technology is preferred &nbsp; 
 - Exposure to real-time data systems and performance at scale. &nbsp; 

Why this role&nbsp; 

You're not inheriting a legacy system or slotting into a layer of management. You're the founding technical voice of a company at the moment it goes to market - with a product already proven on live capital, an experienced team to lead, and the mandate to build it properly. &nbsp; 

Package&nbsp; 

Competitive salary, commensurate with experience. &nbsp;

