Rayvector Technologies builds precision vision systems and automation platforms deployed in demanding semiconductor and industrial environments. We are looking for a mid-level QA Engineer with hands-on experience validating embedded software, camera and vision system integrations, and complex protocol-level communications. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

This role sits at the intersection of hardware-aware software testing and system integration validation. You will own test strategy, execution, and defect lifecycle management across multiple subsystems - working closely with embedded software engineers, system architects, and the program management team. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

Test Planning & Strategy&nbsp; 

- Design and maintain test plans, test cases, and traceability matrices covering functional, integration, regression, and boundary testing&nbsp; 
 - Define test coverage for embedded software features, hardware-software interfaces, and system-level workflows&nbsp; 
 - Participate in design and requirement reviews to identify testability gaps early in the development cycle&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Camera & Vision Systems Testing&nbsp; 

- Validate camera initialization, configuration, frame acquisition, and image quality parameters against defined specifications&nbsp; 
 - Test vision system pipelines including exposure control, focus calibration, and image capture consistency across varying conditions&nbsp; 
 - Verify correctness of OpenCV-based processing outputs - stitching, alignment, and defect detection results&nbsp; 
 - Execute hardware-in-the-loop tests involving camera modules, light controllers, and embedded compute platforms&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Software & API Testing&nbsp; 

- Validate REST API contracts - request/response correctness, error handling, edge cases, and performance under load&nbsp; 
 - Test Angular-based frontend interfaces for functional correctness, state management, and integration with backend services&nbsp; 
 - Build and maintain automated test suites using Python or equivalent scripting for API and regression coverage&nbsp; 
 - Perform negative testing, boundary analysis, and stress testing on system services&nbsp; &nbsp; 

System Integration & Protocol Validation&nbsp; 

- Validate SECS/GEM communication flows - host-equipment message sequences, event reporting, and alarm handling per SEMI standards&nbsp; 
 - Test RTSP/WebRTC streaming pipelines for latency, stability, and frame integrity under real-world network conditions&nbsp; 
 - Verify end-to-end integration across subsystems: EFEM robot control, camera services, light controllers, and the REST API layer&nbsp; 
 - Reproduce and isolate defects at the system integration level; work with engineers to root-cause and verify fixes&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Defect Management & Reporting&nbsp; 

- Log, triage, and track defects with clear reproduction steps, severity classification, and supporting logs or captures&nbsp; 
 - Prepare test summary reports, release sign-off documentation, and quality metrics for program review meetings&nbsp; 
 - Maintain test environments and manage test data for repeatable, deterministic execution&nbsp; 

What We're Looking For&nbsp; 

Must-Have&nbsp; 

- B. Tech in ECE, CS, EE, or a related engineering discipline&nbsp; 
 - 2-4 years of QA/testing experience in embedded software or systems engineering environments&nbsp; 
 - Hands-on experience testing REST APIs - using tools such as Postman, cURL, or custom scripts&nbsp; 
 - Working knowledge of Linux-based environments; comfortable with CLI, log analysis, and shell scripting&nbsp; 
 - Experience with Python for test automation or test tooling&nbsp; 
 - Strong analytical thinking - able to break down complex system interactions into discrete, verifiable test scenarios&nbsp; 
 - Familiarity with defect tracking and project management tools (Zoho, Jira, or equivalent)&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Good to Have&nbsp; 

- Exposure to SECS/GEM protocols or SEMI standards for semiconductor equipment communication&nbsp; 
 - Experience testing video streaming protocols - RTSP, WebRTC, or GStreamer pipelines&nbsp; 
 - Familiarity with camera SDKs, GenICam/GigE Vision, or OpenCV-based image processing&nbsp; 
 - Experience with NVIDIA Jetson platforms or ARM-based embedded Linux systems&nbsp; 
 - Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and integrating automated tests into build workflows&nbsp; 
 - Exposure to air-gapped or offline deployment environments&nbsp; 

Technology Stack You'll Test&nbsp; 

- Embedded compute: NVIDIA Jetson AGX Orin, Orin NX (JetPack 6. x, ARM64)&nbsp; 
 - Vision systems: camera modules, light controllers, OpenCV image processing pipelines&nbsp; 
 - Backend: C++ REST API services, Angular frontend&nbsp; 
 - Protocols: SECS/GEM (SEMI E5/E30/E37), RTSP, WebRTC&nbsp; 
 - Integration: EFEM robot interfaces, multi-subsystem orchestration&nbsp; 
 - OS / Environment: Ubuntu Linux, air-gapped deployment setups&nbsp; 

What We Offer&nbsp; 

- Deep technical exposure to vision systems and semiconductor automation - a rare combination in QA roles&nbsp; 
 - Direct collaboration with embedded engineers and system architects on complex, high-stakes products&nbsp; 
 - A quality-first engineering culture where QA is a first-class function, not an afterthought&nbsp; 
 - Competitive compensation commensurate with experience&nbsp;

