About the role
We are building the next generation platform for continuous integration and delivery at Tesco. Our mission is to upgrade the CI process and provide our engineering teams with a reliable, secure, observable, and predictable CI/CD experience. We are also engaged in developing standard libraries to be used by all container teams to support robust communication mechanism (event based) between containers, securing containers and other common tooling so that we together can deliver high quality, standard and performant applications. &nbsp; 
You will be responsible for
You'll be part of an agile, industry leading team of engineers. You will be contributing to libraries development, creating the future continuous integration and delivery libraries/tools for our area, solving problems, and developing new features through quality, scalable, performant, reliable and maintainable technical solutions. The solutions that you will be responsible for will have impact on hundreds of thousands of Tesco colleagues. Your contribution will have a direct impact on how we build, release, and monitor our applications in ppe, qa and production. Leveraging on tools like Kubernetes, Docker, Shell Script, Ansible, Grafana and others, and services like Azure Cloud, Azure DevOps, you will be responsible for the success of many other talented engineers on their journey to deliver high quality, performant applications. Whilst specific responsibilities will be dependent upon the changing needs of the Tesco business, the following provides an overview of the role's key responsibilities and measures: Focus on libraries development and enhancements, including building/enhancing libraries/tools which can assist to bring more stability continuous integrationFocus on performance, availability, reliability, and security. Effectively communicate your progress to your team members, your manager and wider Tesco colleagues. &nbsp; 

